From: ShadowLink Contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 15:43:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Professional rewrite: robustness, bandwidth guard & reliable
 rar

Both bots fully rewritten and verified with real testing in a sandbox
(syntax + import + logic + a full encrypted multi-volume RAR roundtrip +
end-to-end installer simulation on a clean venv).

tg2bale (Telegram -> Bale):
- Pre-download size guard: skip files over Telegram's 20MB bot limit so no
  bandwidth is wasted on undeliverable files (core fix for weak connections)
- Replace bare excepts with specific exception handling (no more swallowed
  KeyboardInterrupt/CancelledError)
- 429/FloodWait-aware messaging with retries and exponential backoff (3/6/9s)
- atomic tempfile.mkstemp instead of deprecated/insecure tempfile.mktemp
- fail-fast env validation with clear messages
- correct per-batch statistics; drop backlog on restart; no temp-file leaks

tele2server (file splitter):
- install_rar(): rar is NOT in Ubuntu default repos; try multiverse then fall
  back to the official rarlab static binary (arch-aware). The old script
  silently failed on Ubuntu 22.04, leaving compression broken
- check rar exit code and surface the real error instead of a vague message
- header-encrypted multi-volume archives (-hp), configurable PART_SIZE_MB
- FloodWait handling on progress edits and document sends
- strict env validation; never leak downloaded files on error paths

installers (both .sh):
- set -Eeuo pipefail with an ERR trap and failure-aware run_silent/spinner
- input validation loops (token format, numeric IDs)
- TERM-safe clear; idempotent reinstall

